{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-29804cd47c324097ac19","statement":"The canonical integral model $\\scrS_{K}(G,X)$ of $\\bfSh_K(G,X)$ satisfies the following properties.\n\n- If $\\bfSh_K(G,X)$ is proper over $E$, then $\\scrS_K(G,X)$ is proper over $\\mO_{E,(v)}$.\n\n- If $K'=K_p(K^p)'\\subset K=K_pK^p$ where $(K^p)'\\subset K^p$ is an prime-to-$p$ open subgroup, then $\\bfSh_{K'}(G,X)\\to \\bfS_K(G,X)$ is finite \\'etale.\n\n- If $\\mP$ is reductive (so $K_p$ is hyperspecial), then $\\scrS_K(G,X)$ is smooth.\n\n- The canonical morphism $\\rg(\\bfSh_K(G,X)_{\\overline\\bQ_p},\\La)\\to \\rg(\\Sh_K(G,X),R\\Psi)$ is an isomorphism, where $R\\Psi$ denotes the sheaf of nearby cycles of $\\scrS_K(G,X)$.\n\n- There is a morphism\n\n\\begin{equation}\n\\loc_p: \\Sh_K(G,X)\\to \\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}^\\loc,\n\\end{equation}\n\nsuch that the composed morphism\n\n\\[\n\\loc_p(m,n): \\Sh_K(G,X)\\to \\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}^{\\loc(m,n)},\n\\]\n\nis coh. smooth. Here $\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}^{\\loc(m,n)}$ is defined as in <<ref:eq:restr local Sht>>.\nIn addition, if $\\bff\\subset\\overline{\\bff'}\\subset \\overline{\\bfa}$, the following diagram is Cartesian\n\n\\[\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh_{K'}(G,X)\\ar[r]\\ar[d] & \\Sht_{\\mP',\\mu^*}^{\\loc}\\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Sh_{K}(G,X) \\ar[r] & \\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}^{\\loc}.\n}\\]\n\n- The sheaf $(\\loc_p)^!\\delta^!\\mZ_{\\mu}$ is canonically isomorphic to $R\\Psi[d]$, where $d=\\dim\\bfSh_K(G,X)$, where $\\mZ_\\mu$ is the central sheaf on $L^+\\mP\\bs LG/L^+\\mP$ corresponding to the irreducible representation of $\\hat{G}$ of highest weight $\\mu$, and $\\delta: \\Sht^{\\loc}_\\mP\\to L^+\\mP\\bs LG/L^+\\mP$ is the morphism as in <<ref:rem: modification direction of Shtuka>>.\n\n- Let $\\Hk_\\bullet(\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*})$ denote the restriction of the Hecke groupoid $\\Hk_\\bullet(\\Sht_{\\mP})$ from <<ref:eq: nth local Hecke stack for Sht>> to $\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}$. Equivalently, $\\Hk_\\bullet(\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*})$ is the \\v{C}ech nerve of $\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*}\\to \\kot_G$. Then $\\Hk_\\bullet(\\Sht_{\\mP,\\mu^*})$ pullbacks back to a groupoid over $\\Sh_K(G,X)$ under the map $\\loc_p$.\n\n- The partial minimal compactification of the Igusa variety $\\mathrm{Ig}_x$ (as review below) is affine. In particular, if $\\bfSh_K(G,X)$ is proper over $E$, then $\\mathrm{Ig}_x$ is affine.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"5007eef66e455acf568133b81acac726fe3e39b6e755275602af404206d1ca13","kind":"result","label":"Result 406","ref_key":"thm: integral model of Shimura","name":"","order":576,"deps":[{"ref":"eq: nth local Hecke stack for Sht","card_id":"ma-c-cd72c81fe9e742caf340","label":"Equation  nth local Hecke stack for Sht","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq:restr local Sht","card_id":"ma-c-67bf910cc13baebc16c6","label":"Equation restr local Sht","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"rem: modification direction of Shtuka","card_id":"ma-c-3695fbe98287a226724d","label":"Remark 119","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":12343,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":2098,"math_hints":243}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will 